WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.260
- It seemed like everyone and their mother

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:03.390
was advertising Established
Titles this year.

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.460
Is it a scam? Yes.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.140
Is it illegal? Maybe.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.720
Established titles has taken over YouTube.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:10.800
It's extremely prominent.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.810
YouTubers have run
sponsorships for the company,

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:13.830
and the money was flowing.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.800
Like many YouTubers, I had
been approached repeatedly

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.140
about running an Established
Titles sponsorship.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.000
- If it's not Scottish, it's crap!

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.740
- I declined because it
didn't make much sense to me

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.290
and started researching
my own video on the topic.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:27.060
And that wasn't until Scott Schafer made

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.980
a video calling Established Titles a scam.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.150
It pretty much blew up the internet.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.190
This company is a complete scam.

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:35.310
So is established titles really a scam?

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:37.380
Well, that's what we're
gonna figure out here today.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:38.580
Now, it's actually hard to explain

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.540
what Established Titles does

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.940
without already jumping
into value judgements.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.460
So I'll let Established Titles
explain in its own words.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.750
Established Titles owns less

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.910
than 200 acres of land in rural Scotland.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:49.290
Their website says that you can buy

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:52.200
a dedicated one-foot by
one-foot square souvenir plot

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.280
of land from them.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.547
And it also states that you can quote,

00:00:54.547 --> 00:00:56.670
"Become a Lord or lady today."

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:58.281
They say that their packages are quote,

00:00:58.281 --> 00:01:01.008
"Based on a historic Scottish
land ownership custom

00:01:01.008 --> 00:01:04.489
where landowner have been
long referred to as lairds,

00:01:04.489 --> 00:01:06.215
the Scottish term for lord,

00:01:06.215 --> 00:01:08.096
with the female equivalent being lady."

00:01:08.096 --> 00:01:09.595
Okay, so let's start at the beginning.

00:01:09.595 --> 00:01:11.262
When you're talking
about false advertising,

00:01:11.262 --> 00:01:12.633
or fraud in commerce,

00:01:12.633 --> 00:01:14.169
you're probably talking
about one of two laws.

00:01:14.169 --> 00:01:17.477
Section 43(A) of the Lanham
Act authorizes civil suits

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:19.000
for false advertising that quote,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.266
"Misrepresents the nature,
characteristics, qualities,

00:01:21.266 --> 00:01:23.284
or geographic origin,"
of goods or services.

00:01:23.284 --> 00:01:25.326
States have their own laws
regulating false advertising

00:01:25.326 --> 00:01:26.763
and other deceptive trade practices.

00:01:26.763 --> 00:01:28.200
For example, California Business

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.522
and Professions Code 17-500,
aka False Advertising Law,

00:01:31.522 --> 00:01:34.321
or the FAL, prohibits false
and misleading statements

00:01:34.321 --> 00:01:35.154
generally in connection

00:01:35.154 --> 00:01:38.381
with any goods, services, and/or
real or personal property.

00:01:38.381 --> 00:01:39.454
Now to understand whether advertising

00:01:39.454 --> 00:01:41.411
is false or misleading, you have to look

00:01:41.411 --> 00:01:42.863
at the claims that are being made.

00:01:42.863 --> 00:01:44.340
When it comes to established titles,

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:46.523
there are several different
sources of potential claims,

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:49.689
their website advertisements
and YouTube sponsorships.

00:01:49.689 --> 00:01:51.604
And we'll look at each of those in turn.

00:01:51.604 --> 00:01:52.896
(digital glass smashes)

00:01:52.896 --> 00:01:54.564
Well, the homepage and
the hero banner states

00:01:54.564 --> 00:01:56.413
that you can quote, "Save
the Scottish woodlands,"

00:01:56.413 --> 00:01:58.642
and quote, "Become a Lord today."

00:01:58.642 --> 00:01:59.733
A prior version of the website said,

00:01:59.733 --> 00:02:01.755
"Become a Lord or lady today."

00:02:01.755 --> 00:02:03.944
You can quote, "Purchase
a personal lordship

00:02:03.944 --> 00:02:07.015
or ladyship title pack with
dedicated land in Scotland."

00:02:07.015 --> 00:02:08.890
The asterisks direct you
to fine print right below.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:10.628
It says, I quote, "This is a purchase

00:02:10.628 --> 00:02:13.267
for a personal dedication
for a souvenir plot of land.

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:14.891
You may choose to title yourself

00:02:14.891 --> 00:02:17.198
with a title of lord, laird, or lady."

00:02:17.198 --> 00:02:18.980
And as I said before,
the website states quote,

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:20.854
"This is based on a historic
Scottish land ownership custom

00:02:20.854 --> 00:02:23.966
where landowners have been
long referred to as lairds,

00:02:23.966 --> 00:02:25.310
the Scottish term for lord

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:26.760
with the female equivalent being lady."

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.147
On the purchase page, it states quote,

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:30.270
"Each lord title pack includes

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.760
a dedicated plot of land
measuring one square foot,

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.650
five square feet or 10 square feet,

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:36.450
a personalized title
certificate with your name

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:38.010
or the name of the title holder,

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.450
a unique plot number that will

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.220
be assigned to the title holder.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.900
Your digital certificate will be emailed

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.250
to you within 24 hours.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.230
We plant a tree for every order,

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.390
a digital personalized member's handbook."

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.400
Additionally, they have an
entire terms of service page

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.320
on the website as well,
with further detail.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.190
Now, taking this all together,

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.530
there is an implication that by purchasing

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:57.240
a small plot of land
through Established Titles,

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.650
you become officially recognized

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:00.270
as a Scottish noble or lord.

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:01.620
They don't explicitly state that,

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:03.840
and in many ways they
explicitly walk that back.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:05.460
And there's also, an implication of owning

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.140
a piece of Scottish real estate.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:08.340
I'd call that ambiguous,

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:09.450
but we'll talk about that later.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:10.470
Now, they do explicitly state

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:11.400
that you can buy a certificate,

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.900
that you get a dedicated plot of land,

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.090
and that they plant a
tree for every purchase.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.140
Now, before digging into the claims,

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:17.520
let's clear a few things up.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:18.540
Putting aside for the moment

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.510
whether Established Titles
makes any such claims,

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.220
can you become a lord or lady

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.824
through purchasing Scottish
land, novelty or otherwise?

00:03:25.824 --> 00:03:27.240
No, not like this.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.070
Now first off, I am
not a lawyer in the UK,

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:31.380
or a barrister, or a
solicitor, or an advocate,

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:33.440
or any of the other
strange words that they use

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.820
in the ridiculous English legal system.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:38.537
- [Crowd] It's called soccer!
(clapping hands rhythmically)

00:03:38.537 --> 00:03:40.140
It's called soccer!

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:42.990
- The entire idea of nobility
or listening to anything

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:46.860
that this guy says is silly
and quite frankly un-American.

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:47.940
But there is an authority

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:50.310
on this particular ridiculous subject,

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:52.050
that is the Court of the Lord Lyon.

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:53.550
Which deals with all matters relating

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:55.800
to Scottish heraldry and coats of arms.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.097
And that court said, quote,

00:03:57.097 --> 00:03:59.490
"Ownership of a souvenir
plot of land does not bring

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:00.930
with it the right to any description,

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:02.370
such as laird, lord or lady.

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:04.620
laird is not a title,
but a description applied

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:06.570
by those living on and around the estate,

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:08.820
many of whom will derive
their living from it,

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:11.880
to the principal landowner
of a long named area of land.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:14.160
It will therefore be seen
that it is not a description

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:15.390
which is appropriate for the owner

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:16.830
of a normal residential property.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.270
It cannot properly be used to describe

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:20.880
a person who owns a small part
of a larger piece of land.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:22.980
The term laird is not one recognizable

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:24.660
by attachment to a personal name,

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.400
and thus there is no official recognition

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.260
of X-Y laird of Z.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:29.850
The words lord and lady apply to those

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:31.500
on whom peerage has been confirmed,

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.540
and do not relate to
the ownership of land.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.070
Ownership of a souvenir plot of land

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:36.720
is not sufficient to bring a person,

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.730
otherwise ineligible
within the justification

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:41.550
of the Lord Lyon for
seeking a coat of arms."

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:44.430
But what about that historic
Scottish land ownership custom

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:46.320
that Established Titles talks about?

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.000
Well, that's just wrong too.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.770
A representative of the
Court of Lord Lyon stated

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:52.800
in response to another
Established Titles-styled company.

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.350
Quote, "The title, laird of
Glencairn would only apply

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.810
to the owner of the entire
estate if it exists,

00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:59.820
not those buying one foot portions of it."

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.550
Now, you can become a lord
or lady through inheritance,

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.140
or marriage or royal decree,

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:06.990
but not from a Black Friday
sale from Established Titles.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:08.820
A monarch can give a person a peerage,

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:12.120
such as a duke, marques,
earl, viscount or baron.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:15.000
And sometimes people with
hereditary titles sell them,

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.860
usually because they
have financial problems.

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:19.590
These titles sell for tens
of thousands of dollars.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:22.020
Okay, but what about the
implication of land ownership?

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:22.950
Do you own the land?

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:24.510
Now, again, putting aside the issue

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:27.150
of whether Established Titles
makes this particular claim

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:28.830
that you are actually buying the land,

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:30.420
are you actually buying the land?

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:33.120
Well Established Titles
has just under 200 acres.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:34.410
Now, I looked around and rural land

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:37.650
in Scotland can cost
about $10,000 per acre.

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:40.200
Therefore, Established
Titles' several hundred acres

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:41.817
probably cost around $2 million.

00:05:41.817 --> 00:05:43.410
And funny enough, Katerina Yip,

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:47.490
the CEO of Established Titles
also runs LandAssets.com,

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:49.290
which sells real land in Scotland

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:51.270
in one to two acre parcels.

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:52.103
Now, my guess here,

00:05:52.103 --> 00:05:53.640
and this is just pure speculation,

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:55.410
is that they probably
buy up the land in bulk,

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:57.360
and either use it for Established Titles,

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:01.260
or sell it in slightly larger
chunks as actual real estate.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.990
So with respect to the one
foot by one foot parcels,

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:05.670
no, you don't own the land.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.470
It's too small to be
registered in Scotland

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:08.550
and get a deed for it.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:10.500
Instead, you get a contractual dedication

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:11.640
from Established Titles.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.380
This means basically nothing.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.630
It's like buying an MP3 from Apple Music.

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:17.370
You have a contract that they will provide

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:19.350
a certain thing to you, a song.

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:21.210
Do you own it? No, no you don't.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:22.350
Not in any real sense.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:23.820
Now in this context, the Journal of

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.537
the Law Society of Scotland says, quote,

00:06:25.537 --> 00:06:27.570
"There have been a few
articles in the media recently

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:29.910
about companies who were
selling off tiny pieces of land,

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.070
known as souvenir plots in the Highlands.

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:34.500
Some websites suggest that
ownership of the plot carries

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:37.290
with at the right to use the
title of laird, lord or lady.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:38.640
Given that some websites claim

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:42.330
that the Land Registration
Scotland Act of 1979 removes

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.430
the normal requirements
to register your land,

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:47.400
thus permitting the sale to
take place under contract law,

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:49.170
the keeper would like
to clarify her position

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:50.010
on the subject."

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.000
A souvenir plot is defined

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.190
in the Land Registration
Scotland Act of 1979

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:55.800
as a piece of land which
being of inconsiderable size,

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:57.930
or no practical utility is unlikely

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:59.430
to be wanted in isolation except

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:00.690
for the sake of mere ownership,

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:03.930
or for sentimental reasons,
or commemorative purposes.

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:06.000
The keeper is required
to reject an application

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.070
for registration in the land registry

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.720
if the land to which it relates meets

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:11.640
the description of souvenir plot.

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:12.870
However, the fact that the keeper

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:15.330
is obliged to reject the registration does

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.220
not necessarily mean that ownership can

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:19.110
be obtained by some other means.

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:20.640
A real right of ownership
in land in the sense

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.650
of a right that is enforceable
against third parties

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:25.110
can only be obtained by
registration in the Land registry,

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:26.730
or by recording a deed in

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:29.250
the Register of Sasines as appropriate.

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:31.140
Solicitors who are consulted by a client

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:33.690
in relation to the purchase
of a potential souvenir plot

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:35.220
should bear in mind that in some cases

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:38.610
the land in question might
not be of inconsiderable size.

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:41.400
In such cases, no exemption
from registration applies.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:43.470
In other words, the Land Registry Act

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:45.450
that Established Titles relies on defines

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:47.940
a souvenir plot of land in
the context of the things

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:51.240
that the register of land
will necessarily reject.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:52.530
It doesn't affirmatively mean

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:53.730
that a souvenir plot of land

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:56.520
is something the law
will actually recognize.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:59.460
All it means is that it
won't qualify as real estate.

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:01.710
What you get at most is a personal right,

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:02.850
a contractual right against

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:05.130
the actual landowner
of Established Titles.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.380
You do not get a real
ownership of interest.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:08.970
That is you don't own the land.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:10.590
Established titles is
make a contract with you

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.750
that they won't develop your
tiny portion of the land,

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:16.410
and will record your name in
their own private registry.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:19.050
You know what? (laughs)

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:20.670
They're actually making land NFTs.

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:21.990
That's basically what they're doing.

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:23.070
And then next there's a question

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:26.010
of does Established Titles
plant the trees that they claim?

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:27.540
Well, sort of, yes.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:28.890
The very first headline on the website

00:08:28.890 --> 00:08:30.540
is Save the Scottish Woodlands.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:32.610
They also report to plant
a tree with every purchase.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:34.290
Many people have assumed that this means

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:35.670
that the company is planting a tree

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:37.703
on the tiny plots of land
that is assigned to them.

00:08:37.703 --> 00:08:39.600
I mean, if you read
through the entire website,

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:41.160
it becomes clear that this isn't true.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:42.450
Established Titles donates money

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:44.160
to third parties who plant trees.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:46.110
Now their website is replete
with pictures of forests,

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:47.640
and lists several addresses that appear

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:49.380
to correspond to wooded land in Scotland.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:51.720
And I have no reason to
believe that this is false.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:53.790
Now, for several years the
Established Titles website said

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:56.160
it had donated over 42,000 pounds

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:57.720
to these tree planting services.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:00.120
But suddenly in late November 2022,

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:02.100
they changed their website copy to reflect

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:02.970
that they were responsible

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:05.040
for over two million trees being planted.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:06.420
Now, it's clear when
you look at the language

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:07.470
that they work with third parties

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:08.610
who specialize in tree planting.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:10.290
Now there's nothing
inherently wrong with that.

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:13.410
And in fact, you'd probably
want that delegation of labor.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:15.570
These services could probably
plant trees much cheaper

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:16.560
than anybody else.

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:17.880
Except that the language

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:20.880
that Established Titles
uses is often misleading.

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:23.670
In fact, the CEO admitted that
the language was misleading,

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:25.410
especially when modified by YouTubers.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:28.140
- I think we'll have
to like rephrase that,

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:30.930
or look at what we're saying
and try to make it clearer.

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:32.550
- Okay, but let's go
off on a quick tangent,

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:33.383
if you'll indulge me.

00:09:33.383 --> 00:09:34.590
Let's talk about how much money

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:36.450
does Established Titles make?

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:38.520
Well, the answer I think is a lot.

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:39.630
Established Titles is currently owned

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:40.830
by a venture capital firm based

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:42.600
in Hong Kong called Galton Voysey.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:43.830
It's this company that was reaching out

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:46.590
to YouTubers to do sponsorships
for Established Titles.

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:47.790
Now, I've talked to many creators

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:49.140
and I know that Established Titles

00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:52.470
was sometimes paying five and
six figures for sponsorships.

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:54.750
For the bigger YouTubers
with bigger views,

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:57.900
sometimes 75,000 to
over $100,000 per video.

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:00.990
Sadly, they only offered
me $7,000 per video,

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:04.860
and my friend Rowan, who is
a cardiac surgeon, 3,500.

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:06.870
So you know the lawyers win again.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:09.540
But as it happens, your boy
here isn't just a lawyer,

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:12.270
he's also a content creator
who runs sponsorships,

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:14.340
and is an expert in the creator economy.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:15.173
So let's dig in.

00:10:15.173 --> 00:10:16.710
Let's make some educated guesses about

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:18.690
the business of Established Titles.

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:20.640
In response to all this backlash,

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:22.290
the CEO of Established
Titles wrote a letter

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:25.020
to creators, quote, "Galton
Voysey has supported us

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.760
since day one, even though they knew

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:29.220
that their initial funding
for this conservation project

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:30.960
would most likely lead to financial loss.

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.520
This year alone, Galton Voysey has made

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:35.910
a multimillion dollar loss
on Established Titles.

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:38.850
Sponsoring all those videos isn't cheap."

00:10:38.850 --> 00:10:39.960
And you know what? She's right.

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:42.000
Those sponsorships are expensive.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.470
They've sponsored hundreds of videos

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:46.200
to the tune of four, five,
and six figure deals.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.270
So let's talk about profit or loss.

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:49.830
I'm a little bit skeptical here.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:51.540
Now, as I mentioned,
Established Titles boasts

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.640
of over two million trees being planted

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:54.990
in response to their business.

00:10:54.990 --> 00:10:56.190
We know that the upper limit of

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:59.100
the cost per tree is $1 per tree.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:01.320
That figure comes directly
from One Tree Planted,

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:02.760
the company that Established Titles works

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:03.660
with to plant trees.

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:04.710
Now, I have no reason to think

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:07.560
that either the 42,000
pounds being donated,

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:09.660
or the two million trees numbers is wrong.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:10.800
I suspect that they realize

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:11.910
that two million trees sounds way

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:14.490
more impressive than 42,000 pounds.

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:16.410
So they change the language on
the website to reflect that.

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:17.520
That makes sense.

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:19.290
But because of that, I think
we can easily figure out

00:11:19.290 --> 00:11:21.660
how much of a cash cow
Established Titles is.

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:22.710
They say that they're responsible

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:24.150
for over two million trees.

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:27.510
We know that it costs at most
$1 per tree and probably less.

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:28.890
Now, the minimum that you can spend

00:11:28.890 --> 00:11:32.910
on Established Titles is $50
for a digital only certificate.

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:34.770
If you wanted that printed
out and shipped to you,

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:36.570
that costs an extra $30.

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:38.280
If you want that piece of paper framed,

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:42.180
that costs an extra $59,
for a total of $139.

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:45.330
Now you can also buy larger
plots of land for more money.

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:46.980
But at least the printing
out, and the certificate,

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:50.280
and the frame upsells cost
$30 and $59 respectively,

00:11:50.280 --> 00:11:52.530
with hundreds of dollars in extra upsells

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:54.900
if you want want five or
10 square foot packages,

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:56.220
or a couple's package.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:58.230
Then at the checkout page
you're automatically signed up

00:11:58.230 --> 00:11:59.880
for an $8 recurring charge

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:02.400
to plant one tree per
month until you cancel.

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.890
Now as an aside, I found
this automatic addition

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:06.390
to my cart to be particularly gulling,

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:08.340
because the language makes it sound like

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:09.360
it's the tree planting

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:11.600
that is already included
with your purchase.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:13.620
In other words, when I was checking out,

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:15.540
and yes I did purchase
one of these things,

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:17.760
I thought they listed
the tree with every order

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:19.500
in my cart as a separate item.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:21.240
I had to read the small print to realize

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:24.660
that this was an upsell of
a monthly recurring $8 cost

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:27.210
for one tree being planted every month.

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:28.440
Now the fact that they have planted

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:30.900
over two million trees
means that they've made,

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:33.210
approximately, two
million individual sales.

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:35.070
Now, granted this number might be off

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:37.500
if they made a separate
donation of trees on their own,

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:39.540
but if they had, they'd
probably be shouting it

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:40.500
from the mountain tops.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:42.450
And admittedly, that
upsell of a monthly tree

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:44.850
will drive that dollar
per sale number down.

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:46.260
So let's be extremely conservative,

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:48.810
and say that there are two trees per sale.

00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:51.180
In other words, two million
trees being donated means

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:54.210
that they've sold at least
one million individual sales.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:55.560
So to figure out the revenue and profit,

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:56.820
you can generally multiply the number

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:59.190
of sales roughly two trees per sale

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:00.900
by how much they make on each sale.

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:02.310
So how do we figure that out?

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:04.020
Well, given that the
minimum that you can spend

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:05.070
on a digital certificate

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:07.890
that costs zero marginal dollars is $50,

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:09.360
and the sheer number of upsells

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:12.090
that also cost almost
zero marginal dollars,

00:13:12.090 --> 00:13:13.740
I think that the average cart value

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:15.780
is easily $100 plus.

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:16.740
Now factor in fulfillment

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:18.450
of maybe a couple dollars per order

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:20.130
for a cheap frame in shipping,

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.990
then take some off the top for overhead.

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:24.810
Then the biggest expense is
marketing the sponsorships.

00:13:24.810 --> 00:13:27.270
Now, it's not unusual to
spend 30 to 50% of revenue

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:28.680
on marketing for a high margin,

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:30.690
instant profit product like this.

00:13:30.690 --> 00:13:32.610
And then they probably
spent about $2 million

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:34.350
on 200 acres in Scotland.

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:36.360
All told they're probably
looking at revenue

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:38.550
of roughly $100 per purchase,

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:41.460
and a net profit of
about $50 per purchase.

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:42.840
Yes, that probably means that over

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.340
the last three years they have revenue

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.260
of roughly $100 million,

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:48.777
with profit easily exceeding $50 million.

00:13:48.777 --> 00:13:50.130
But look, that's just a guess.

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:52.290
My assumptions could be wrong.
You can do the math yourself.

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:53.730
But at base I think Established Titles

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:56.370
is wildly profitable with a
large expense being marketing.

00:13:56.370 --> 00:13:57.600
But the benefit of that marketing

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:59.670
is that you can easily
scale it up or down,

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:01.020
and make instant profit.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.700
And they could easily be making $2

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:04.170
for every $1 that they spent.

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:05.760
They clearly make a large margin

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:07.770
on every single sale that they make.

00:14:07.770 --> 00:14:08.940
And there's even a plaque.

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:11.400
On Galton Voysey's office
tour in their website.

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:13.770
We see that even as far
back as 2020 and 2021,

00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:16.560
before this huge boom
in YouTube sponsorships,

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:18.300
Established Titles was regularly making

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:20.640
over a million dollars
in quarterly profit,

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:22.410
and it was their most profitable company.

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:23.670
So now we get to the heart of the matter.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:24.930
Does Established Titles engage

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:27.270
in false or misleading advertisements?

00:14:27.270 --> 00:14:29.640
Their website states right in
front, "Become a Lord Today."

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:32.160
And that's not technically
true. You can't become a lord.

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:33.780
The implication is that Established Titles

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:35.190
has found this one weird trick,

00:14:35.190 --> 00:14:36.840
this funny little legal loophole

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:38.730
that lets you become Scottish nobility.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:41.040
But implications are not
necessarily false advertising.

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:42.210
And there is subsequent language

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:44.160
that claws this back
further down on the website.

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:45.360
And they say that it's based on,

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:49.350
but not necessarily following
an ancient Scottish custom.

00:14:49.350 --> 00:14:50.760
And they say that it's a purchase

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:53.760
for a personal dedication
for a souvenir plot of land.

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:55.590
And you may choose to title yourself

00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:57.450
with the title of lord, laird or lady.

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:59.460
And it's true that they will dedicate,

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:02.190
whatever that means,
a plot of land to you.

00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:03.360
They imply that you own the land,

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:04.620
though they don't outright say that.

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:07.500
And that historic custom
language is weird though.

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:10.080
Where landowners have been
long referred to as lairds,

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:11.160
the Scottish term for lord,

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:13.140
with the female equivalent being lady.

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:15.870
I mean in what sense? You're
not really buying the land.

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:17.970
So why is this custom even relevant,

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.260
or being displayed on the website?

00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:21.600
I mean obviously, we know why it's there,

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:23.250
but syntactically, what is it doing?

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:25.380
But look, there are good
arguments on both sides here.

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:26.580
From Established Titles' side,

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:28.980
the purchaser does get
certain rights related

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:29.970
to their plot of land.

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:32.190
Yip explains that should
Established Titles ever attempt

00:15:32.190 --> 00:15:33.870
to sell the land that your square foot

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:35.850
is on you can sue them.

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:37.440
While you don't actually get a deed

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:38.490
or a plot registration

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:40.920
by possessing some contractual
rights over the square,

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:43.380
you do, to some degree, own that land.

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:45.330
Now the bit about becoming
a lord is a fun premise,

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:46.980
but it's pretty silly once you realize

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:48.900
that it would mean that literally anyone

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:51.960
that owned land in Scotland
would be a lord or a lady,

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:53.580
which doesn't make any sense.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:55.920
- Well, it's a well known fact, Sunny Jim,

00:15:55.920 --> 00:15:57.570
that there's a secret society of

00:15:57.570 --> 00:15:59.700
the five wealthiest
people in the world known

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:03.090
as The Pentaverate who run everything

00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:05.940
in the world including the newspapers.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:08.970
And meet tri-annually at
a Secret Country Mansion

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:12.090
in Colorado known as, The Meadows.

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:13.800
- But that leads into
one of the best defenses,

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:16.980
which would be that it's
so ridiculous on its face

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:19.620
that no one would be confused
about what they were buying.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:21.090
No one seriously thought

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:23.970
that they were actually going
to become Scottish nobility.

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:28.020
- Ah, I hated the colonel
with his wee, beady eyes!

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:28.980
- And their website is pretty clear

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:31.230
about implying a real noble title,

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:32.490
but never actually saying it.

00:16:32.490 --> 00:16:34.860
And then, you know, having lots and lots

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:37.080
of disclaimers to claw that back anyway.

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:38.070
But it's funny, you know,

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:39.840
once I started researching
Established Titles,

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:42.330
I started getting tons
of targeted advertising.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:45.270
And in this case, it was
actually very helpful.

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.550
In these two targeted ads that I received,

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:48.810
there were even bigger gaps

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:49.890
between what was advertised

00:16:49.890 --> 00:16:52.020
and what consumers were actually getting.

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:53.400
- [Wife] When you buy land in Scotland you

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:55.800
are legally referred to as a lord or lady.

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:57.870
So this, I bought a square foot of land,

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:59.297
where they're gonna plant a tree.

00:16:59.297 --> 00:17:00.270
(husband laughs)

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:04.083
So you are legally
referred to as Lord Liam.

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:09.030
- The advertisement state
with zero qualifications

00:17:09.030 --> 00:17:11.280
that you will own a specific unit of land

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:13.890
in Scotland with your
purchase and become a lord.

00:17:13.890 --> 00:17:15.120
That advertisement has nothing

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:17.400
about getting a contractual
right to a dedication.

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:18.840
And the ad also implies causation

00:17:18.840 --> 00:17:21.090
between buying a piece of land, false,

00:17:21.090 --> 00:17:23.220
and then becoming a lord, also false.

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:24.540
But in fairness, Established Titles' terms

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:26.130
and conditions clarify these claims

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:28.147
on the website in small
prints saying, quote,

00:17:28.147 --> 00:17:29.220
"The purchase of a title pack

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:31.200
from Established Titles
does not constitute

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:34.230
or trigger a transfer of
ownership over that souvenir plot

00:17:34.230 --> 00:17:36.237
or any part of the land
in the legal sense."

00:17:36.237 --> 00:17:37.560
And the website also describes

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:40.050
this lord package as quote,
"A fun novelty product."

00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:42.300
Though it is pretty sneaky
that they titled their products

00:17:42.300 --> 00:17:46.470
a Lordship package and a Ladyship package,

00:17:46.470 --> 00:17:50.130
without actually bestowing
a lordship or a ladyship.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:52.477
But the website also describes
these packages as quote,

00:17:52.477 --> 00:17:54.120
"A fun novelty product

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:56.640
that the purchase is a personal dedication

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:58.170
for a souvenir plot of land.

00:17:58.170 --> 00:18:00.510
And the individual quote may choose

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:03.270
to title yourself with the
title of lord, laird or lady.

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:05.100
But arguably these disclosures contradict

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:06.240
the plain text to these ads,

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:07.950
which say that you will own Scottish land

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:10.200
and you will become a
lord with your purchase.

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:13.200
And contradicting the plain
text of an advertisement

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:15.510
is a no-no when it comes
to false advertising.

00:18:15.510 --> 00:18:17.130
And furthermore, the ad's inclusion

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:19.200
of a formal certificate
gives the impression

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.730
that a person buying a certificate

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:24.030
will literally be a lord
or lady of Scottish land.

00:18:24.030 --> 00:18:26.550
But hold on, because some
of their ads are even worse,

00:18:26.550 --> 00:18:28.290
and I have the receipts.

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:29.280
More on that in a second.

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:30.480
And a lot of people have noted

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:33.180
that Established Titles'
business evokes comparisons

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:35.880
with the famous register of Star Company.

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:37.950
Where basically you're
just paying this company,

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:40.050
so you can put your name associated

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:42.570
with some star in, again,
a private registry.

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:46.530
Not the official place where
stars are actually named.

00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:48.840
But while a person literally can't own

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:50.370
a piece of the galaxy,

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:52.110
becoming a lord is a real thing

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:54.030
that you can do in real life.

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:56.070
And again, the clear implication

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:57.630
of Established Titles' advertisements

00:18:57.630 --> 00:18:59.370
is that if you pay them money,

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:01.470
you will literally
become a lord or a lady.

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:02.700
And in fact, in the FAQ section

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.140
of Established Titles' website,

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:05.820
the company encourages purchasers to refer

00:19:05.820 --> 00:19:08.190
to themselves as lords or
ladies on official documents,

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:10.920
including credit cards
and airline tickets.

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:12.450
Now I got a hold of the creator brief

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:13.680
that Established Titles gave

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:15.540
to various YouTube creators

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:17.880
when they were running
Established Titles sponsorships.

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:21.420
And in that brief Established
Titles says specifically

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:23.910
that the creator can't say
that you can change your name

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:26.430
on your passport or when
applying for bank loans.

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:28.590
And as the CEO confirmed in
an interview the reason is,

00:19:28.590 --> 00:19:30.390
because there isn't a dropdown menu

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:32.580
when you're choosing your
options on a passport.

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:36.030
In most common law jurisdictions,
you can title yourself,

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:37.590
however you wanna title yourself,

00:19:37.590 --> 00:19:39.450
as long as you're not well,

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:40.920
as long as you're doing it in good faith,

00:19:40.920 --> 00:19:44.670
and you're not using it
to try to get a bank loan.

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:49.110
Or try to get someone
to invest like way more

00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:52.170
than they would've, you
know, trying to make

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:54.240
yourself seem trustworthy,

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:59.240
and make someone else basically
give you funds for that

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:05.660
by using the word sorry,
using the lord or lady title.

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.160
But if you're doing it in good faith,

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:10.080
if you're putting it
on like a plane ticket,

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:11.310
or a credit card,

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:12.720
you can technically call yourself,

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:14.550
whatever you wanna call yourself.

00:20:14.550 --> 00:20:16.110
Rather, sorry, very specifically,

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:18.870
you can title yourself however
you wanna title yourself.

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:20.580
- But if it's not actually possible,

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:22.950
why you need to warn
people not to do that?

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:24.480
And then they say that you can't do

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:25.740
it when applying for a bank loan,

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:29.310
because you can't seem to be
more trustworthy than you are,

00:20:29.310 --> 00:20:31.020
and you can only do things in good faith.

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:33.960
But under one circumstances
can you ever say

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:36.480
that you are a lord or a
lady in good faith based

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:38.820
on Established Titles' products.

00:20:38.820 --> 00:20:40.380
It's either a joke or a gimmick,

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:42.360
or you can do it in good
faith, it can't be both.

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:43.800
So that takes us to the defenses.

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:46.470
Established Titles has vigorously
pushed back against claims

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:48.630
that it has engaged in false
or deceptive advertising,

00:20:48.630 --> 00:20:50.130
and is otherwise a scam.

00:20:50.130 --> 00:20:52.650
And admittedly, they have strong defenses.

00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:56.010
After Scott Shafer's video
on November 24, 2022,

00:20:56.010 --> 00:20:58.560
the founder of Established
Titles, Katerina Yip,

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:00.330
sent a letter to creators.

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:01.560
And she described the package

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:03.750
as a fun gift meant for a good laugh.

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:05.670
Miss Yip further states that its consumers

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:07.440
to understand that they
aren't literally becoming

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:08.700
a Scottish lord or lady.

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:11.370
Suggesting any belief to the
contrary would be unreasonable.

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:13.710
Quote, "We have always been
clear that our certificates

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:15.750
are based on a historic Scottish custom

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:18.150
of calling landowners
lairds, lords or ladies.

00:21:18.150 --> 00:21:20.340
And that it does not grant
you the right to rule,

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:22.440
or make you a member of any royal family,

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:23.850
nor the right to a peerage."

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:25.920
And there's no doubt that
a lot of people saw this

00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:28.050
as a gag gift, and therefore did not buy.

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:29.760
That's not false advertising.

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:31.530
That could be described
as accurate advertising,

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:34.200
and people making a reasonable
decision not to purchase.

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:35.340
Now, a friend of mine who ran

00:21:35.340 --> 00:21:37.410
an established title spot,
explained it like this.

00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:39.270
Quote, "I'm sure from
a lawyer perspective,

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:41.970
you're pulling your hair out
at the, you can own land claim.

00:21:41.970 --> 00:21:44.580
But I think the rest of us think
of this as a silly gimmick,

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:46.920
a feature or bug of late stage capitalism

00:21:46.920 --> 00:21:49.410
where people are looking to
spend their disposable income

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:52.170
on weird like feeling a part
of some souvenir plot of land

00:21:52.170 --> 00:21:54.750
in a beautiful far away
place that feels formal,

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:56.010
and is potentially contributing

00:21:56.010 --> 00:21:57.180
to some preservation effort.

00:21:57.180 --> 00:21:58.380
But I honestly don't even think

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:00.480
the conservation thing is even an appeal.

00:22:00.480 --> 00:22:02.040
People find value in weird stuff.

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:03.390
And again, I don't think anyone

00:22:03.390 --> 00:22:04.613
is earnestly purchasing Established Titles

00:22:04.613 --> 00:22:06.240
through any of their competitors.

00:22:06.240 --> 00:22:09.480
Yes, there are several it appears
thinking they now own land

00:22:09.480 --> 00:22:11.250
and are literally a lord.

00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:12.510
If anyone is selling it like

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:14.010
that I agree that's misleading.

00:22:14.010 --> 00:22:15.960
But it's hard to call
Established Titles snake oil,

00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:18.900
or scam when it's so
clearly a silly gimmick."

00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:22.050
Now, I think this is a totally
fair way of looking at it.

00:22:22.050 --> 00:22:23.460
And it's an interpretation that buoyed

00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:26.400
by all the disclaimers on the
Established Titles website.

00:22:26.400 --> 00:22:29.250
A lot of the critics of
Established Titles saw no value

00:22:29.250 --> 00:22:30.810
in purchasing from Established Titles,

00:22:30.810 --> 00:22:32.250
and therefore didn't purchase.

00:22:32.250 --> 00:22:34.860
But they then assume that
everyone who did purchase

00:22:34.860 --> 00:22:37.560
must have been a complete
idiot, and been misguided.

00:22:37.560 --> 00:22:39.060
But I think my friend's
interpretation recognizes

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:40.110
the agency of the buyers

00:22:40.110 --> 00:22:42.420
and the value propositions
of Established Titles.

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:44.610
And all that is totally reasonable.

00:22:44.610 --> 00:22:46.860
And in a November 2022 interview

00:22:46.860 --> 00:22:49.110
with a British YouTuber,
Katerina Yip states

00:22:49.110 --> 00:22:51.060
that Established Titles
has always classified

00:22:51.060 --> 00:22:53.190
this lord, lady package as a novelty item.

00:22:53.190 --> 00:22:55.740
- We've always been very
clear on the website

00:22:55.740 --> 00:22:57.843
that this is a novelty item.

00:22:58.792 --> 00:23:00.100
And I think that

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:05.940
the language really hasn't
changed since day one.

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:08.160
- But there are some
problems with this defense.

00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:09.570
In that brief they include a section

00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:11.160
on common errors to avoid.

00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:12.577
And section two says, quote,

00:23:12.577 --> 00:23:14.970
"The phrase royalty or nobility.

00:23:14.970 --> 00:23:17.340
Our certificate is based on
a historic Scottish custom

00:23:17.340 --> 00:23:19.560
of calling landowners
lairds/lords or ladies.

00:23:19.560 --> 00:23:21.240
It does not grant you the right to rule,

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:23.610
or make you a member of any royal family.

00:23:23.610 --> 00:23:26.010
Our certificates also do
not grant you peerages

00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:27.300
of the United Kingdom."

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:29.730
Now first, I think that
there's an argument to be made

00:23:29.730 --> 00:23:30.870
that the reason that they have

00:23:30.870 --> 00:23:32.910
to tell creators not to say this is,

00:23:32.910 --> 00:23:34.470
because they know that they're creating

00:23:34.470 --> 00:23:36.180
a lot of confusion in the marketplace.

00:23:36.180 --> 00:23:38.640
Now, arguably people have been misled.

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:40.020
It also undercuts the argument

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:42.510
that the term lord is ambiguous.

00:23:42.510 --> 00:23:44.040
In general, I think it
would be a good defense

00:23:44.040 --> 00:23:46.500
to say that lord or lady is
an ambiguous term subject

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:47.460
to multiple definitions,

00:23:47.460 --> 00:23:49.710
one of which Established Titles meets.

00:23:49.710 --> 00:23:51.120
But I think most people understand it

00:23:51.120 --> 00:23:53.580
to mean the nobility
associated with peerage,

00:23:53.580 --> 00:23:55.290
which Established Titles tells creators,

00:23:55.290 --> 00:23:57.120
specifically, not to say.

00:23:57.120 --> 00:23:58.860
Though, on the other hand,
this is also evidence

00:23:58.860 --> 00:24:00.390
that Established Titles is being careful,

00:24:00.390 --> 00:24:02.160
and affirmatively avoiding confusion.

00:24:02.160 --> 00:24:03.660
But a second problem with this defense

00:24:03.660 --> 00:24:05.610
is that the content creators
who have been sponsored

00:24:05.610 --> 00:24:08.760
by Established Titles often
use the word officially,

00:24:08.760 --> 00:24:10.770
or real in the context of the lordship,

00:24:10.770 --> 00:24:12.540
as in officially a lord.

00:24:12.540 --> 00:24:14.280
Or now, I'm a real lord,

00:24:14.280 --> 00:24:16.140
- [Narrator] Thanks to an
old Scottish custom means

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:18.720
that you or the person you're
buying the land for officially

00:24:18.720 --> 00:24:20.610
becomes what's known as a laird.

00:24:20.610 --> 00:24:23.915
That's a lord or lady for
us modern English speakers.

00:24:23.915 --> 00:24:27.767
- You could officially
become a lord or a lady, too.

00:24:27.767 --> 00:24:31.860
- I am a 100% authentic Scottish lord.

00:24:31.860 --> 00:24:33.810
- [Influencer] This official
certificate making you

00:24:33.810 --> 00:24:35.430
a real lord or lady.

00:24:35.430 --> 00:24:36.720
- I think they use that language,

00:24:36.720 --> 00:24:38.790
which is not included
in the talking points,

00:24:38.790 --> 00:24:41.700
because that's kind of what
it seems like they're selling.

00:24:41.700 --> 00:24:44.940
And I suspect that they
were confused and/or misled.

00:24:44.940 --> 00:24:47.550
And like all sponsors
Established Titles has a duty

00:24:47.550 --> 00:24:49.710
to supervise the sponsorship integration,

00:24:49.710 --> 00:24:50.850
at least the part of the video

00:24:50.850 --> 00:24:52.590
that they have specifically sponsored.

00:24:52.590 --> 00:24:54.360
And according to the
creators that I've talked to,

00:24:54.360 --> 00:24:57.390
they do review every
video before it goes live.

00:24:57.390 --> 00:24:59.520
This is because companies
are legally responsible

00:24:59.520 --> 00:25:01.380
for the portions of the
videos that they sponsor,

00:25:01.380 --> 00:25:04.250
and the words that those
creators say in that context.

00:25:04.250 --> 00:25:06.930
In other words, when a creator
says Established Titles

00:25:06.930 --> 00:25:08.640
will make you a real lord,

00:25:08.640 --> 00:25:11.850
or you'll officially become a
lord, they own that language,

00:25:11.850 --> 00:25:13.380
even though it's arguably contrary

00:25:13.380 --> 00:25:15.180
to the provided talking points.

00:25:15.180 --> 00:25:18.030
Some sponsorships lean into
the conservation aspect.

00:25:18.030 --> 00:25:20.910
But a lot of the
sponsorships on YouTube focus

00:25:20.910 --> 00:25:22.770
on the lordship and many go hard

00:25:22.770 --> 00:25:24.600
on becoming official or real.

00:25:24.600 --> 00:25:26.160
In fact, the CEO admits that this

00:25:26.160 --> 00:25:27.570
is the main criticism of people

00:25:27.570 --> 00:25:30.120
is that the titles are
not official titles.

00:25:30.120 --> 00:25:33.242
And yet, tons of creators use those terms,

00:25:33.242 --> 00:25:35.220
and use that kind of language.

00:25:35.220 --> 00:25:36.750
But where could those creators have gotten

00:25:36.750 --> 00:25:38.160
that wrong idea from?

00:25:38.160 --> 00:25:40.080
Well, remember that I mentioned that there

00:25:40.080 --> 00:25:44.070
were some even worse, more
dubious Established Titles ads?

00:25:44.070 --> 00:25:46.110
Well, here you can see that
Established Titles does

00:25:46.110 --> 00:25:48.420
in fact use the language
of official lordship

00:25:48.420 --> 00:25:50.850
and legal lordship pretty often.

00:25:50.850 --> 00:25:52.140
- [Wife] When you buy land in Scotland,

00:25:52.140 --> 00:25:54.660
you are legally referred
to as a lord or lady.

00:25:54.660 --> 00:25:56.700
So this I bought a square foot of land

00:25:56.700 --> 00:25:58.069
where they're gonna plant a tree.

00:25:58.069 --> 00:25:59.100
(husband laughs)

00:25:59.100 --> 00:26:02.913
So you are legally
referred to as a Lord Liam.

00:26:05.005 --> 00:26:08.850
- Can you guess how I became
a lord at just age 19?

00:26:08.850 --> 00:26:09.683
- No.

00:26:09.683 --> 00:26:10.920
- I would probably have to guess

00:26:10.920 --> 00:26:12.300
that you inherited the position,

00:26:12.300 --> 00:26:14.160
because of your father before you.

00:26:14.160 --> 00:26:16.110
- Actually Established
Titles sells a title

00:26:16.110 --> 00:26:18.140
that can officially make
you a lord or a lady.

00:26:18.140 --> 00:26:20.910
On top of this, since you're
officially a lord or a lady,

00:26:20.910 --> 00:26:22.950
you have dedicated land in Scotland.

00:26:22.950 --> 00:26:24.570
You will literally get a certification

00:26:24.570 --> 00:26:26.100
that makes you a lord or a lady.

00:26:26.100 --> 00:26:26.933
Pretty cool, right?

00:26:26.933 --> 00:26:28.138
- Yeah.

00:26:28.138 --> 00:26:30.258
- (laughs) I'm a lady!

00:26:30.258 --> 00:26:32.541
I have land in Scotland!

00:26:32.541 --> 00:26:35.612
- I love it! I've always
wanted to be a lady.

00:26:35.612 --> 00:26:36.695
- I'm a lady!

00:26:38.213 --> 00:26:39.570
- Hat tip to Scott Schafer

00:26:39.570 --> 00:26:41.550
for finding some of those ridiculous ads.

00:26:41.550 --> 00:26:44.700
And they consistently say that
you officially become a lord,

00:26:44.700 --> 00:26:47.670
or that you are legally
a lord, no disclaimers.

00:26:47.670 --> 00:26:49.200
So while in general established title says

00:26:49.200 --> 00:26:51.450
that you can refer to yourself as a lord,

00:26:51.450 --> 00:26:53.430
and maybe the term lord, laird or lady

00:26:53.430 --> 00:26:55.170
is open to interpretation.

00:26:55.170 --> 00:26:59.100
Claiming that you are officially
a lord, or legally a lord

00:26:59.100 --> 00:27:01.740
is quite another stronger
claim altogether.

00:27:01.740 --> 00:27:03.330
Now, I suspect there are a good number

00:27:03.330 --> 00:27:05.820
of people who read the
Established Titles website or ads,

00:27:05.820 --> 00:27:08.070
and thought, yes, noble titles are silly.

00:27:08.070 --> 00:27:09.870
But according to this legal loophole,

00:27:09.870 --> 00:27:11.670
I can be a real noble, too.

00:27:11.670 --> 00:27:13.320
And if true, that could have been

00:27:13.320 --> 00:27:15.240
the result of misleading advertising.

00:27:15.240 --> 00:27:18.180
In part, I know this because
Established Titles blog

00:27:18.180 --> 00:27:19.267
specifically says, quote,

00:27:19.267 --> 00:27:22.260
"You won't believe this
legal loophole in Scotland."

00:27:22.260 --> 00:27:23.700
I mean, I guess technically that's true,

00:27:23.700 --> 00:27:25.590
because I don't believe them.

00:27:25.590 --> 00:27:26.707
But they go on, quote,

00:27:26.707 --> 00:27:28.560
"There's a small legal
loophole in Scotland

00:27:28.560 --> 00:27:29.880
that makes it possible for anyone

00:27:29.880 --> 00:27:32.190
to title themselves as lord or a lady.

00:27:32.190 --> 00:27:34.140
Through this loophole
anyone can buy a small plot

00:27:34.140 --> 00:27:35.970
of land in Scotland
and refer to themselves

00:27:35.970 --> 00:27:37.410
as a lord or a lady."

00:27:37.410 --> 00:27:39.090
Furthermore, stating that your product

00:27:39.090 --> 00:27:41.520
is a novelty on the website
doesn't necessarily cure

00:27:41.520 --> 00:27:44.460
the issue of Established
Titles' advertising campaigns

00:27:44.460 --> 00:27:46.650
that suggest you
literally become nobility.

00:27:46.650 --> 00:27:49.350
And as the FTC has made very
clear, you cannot advertise

00:27:49.350 --> 00:27:50.670
in one way and have disclaimers

00:27:50.670 --> 00:27:52.560
that say something else on your website,

00:27:52.560 --> 00:27:54.810
particularly if you have
to scroll to find it.

00:27:54.810 --> 00:27:56.970
Now, perhaps it's true
that absolutely no one

00:27:56.970 --> 00:27:59.130
thought they were a real lord or lady.

00:27:59.130 --> 00:28:01.350
But given Established
Titles' marketing campaigns

00:28:01.350 --> 00:28:03.210
and the sponsored creators who suggests

00:28:03.210 --> 00:28:05.160
that this is anything but a novelty,

00:28:05.160 --> 00:28:07.290
I definitely wouldn't hang
my hat on that defense.

00:28:07.290 --> 00:28:09.720
Now, another defense in
Established Titles' favor

00:28:09.720 --> 00:28:11.400
is that people accurately
view this purchase

00:28:11.400 --> 00:28:13.920
from Established Titles as
a pro-conservation gift.

00:28:13.920 --> 00:28:15.420
And as far as I can tell, you do get

00:28:15.420 --> 00:28:17.700
at least one tree planted
with every purchase.

00:28:17.700 --> 00:28:20.700
They probably have purchased
200 acres in Scotland.

00:28:20.700 --> 00:28:23.100
They do work with third
party tree planting services,

00:28:23.100 --> 00:28:24.420
which appear legitimate.

00:28:24.420 --> 00:28:26.160
You're not getting
nothing for your purchase.

00:28:26.160 --> 00:28:28.050
You are contributing
to environmental causes

00:28:28.050 --> 00:28:30.990
with a cheeky nonsense nobility
thing thrown in for kicks.

00:28:30.990 --> 00:28:32.640
The CEO explains what they actually do,

00:28:32.640 --> 00:28:34.320
which isn't necessarily a bad thing,

00:28:34.320 --> 00:28:36.840
buying land and then
contracting to never develop it.

00:28:36.840 --> 00:28:38.640
But when asked about consumer confusion,

00:28:38.640 --> 00:28:40.530
the CEO waffles for almost a full minute,

00:28:40.530 --> 00:28:42.540
trying to dance around
all of the confusion.

00:28:42.540 --> 00:28:47.520
- Do you think that there is
a little bit of unclearness

00:28:47.520 --> 00:28:50.190
in terms of what it is?

00:28:50.190 --> 00:28:52.050
Because essentially you guys are

00:28:52.050 --> 00:28:53.640
the lords and ladies of that land.

00:28:53.640 --> 00:28:55.560
You're the ones who own it.

00:28:55.560 --> 00:29:00.180
So do you think there is a
little bit of misunderstanding,

00:29:00.180 --> 00:29:03.000
or miscommunication do you
think maybe to the audience as

00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:05.790
to what their true status
statuses around that?

00:29:05.790 --> 00:29:08.670
Because I feel like a part of it does rely

00:29:08.670 --> 00:29:11.550
on individuals knowing
the laws around this,

00:29:11.550 --> 00:29:13.590
and not everybody does.

00:29:13.590 --> 00:29:16.110
I certainly didn't. (laughs)

00:29:16.110 --> 00:29:18.030
- That's a really fair question.

00:29:18.030 --> 00:29:21.990
So I think we're very clear about that.

00:29:21.990 --> 00:29:26.283
In our FAQs we talk about
how souvenir plots work,

00:29:27.581 --> 00:29:29.040
and how we take our obligations

00:29:29.040 --> 00:29:32.190
to our lords and ladies very seriously.

00:29:32.190 --> 00:29:35.490
So I wouldn't say that we are the,

00:29:35.490 --> 00:29:36.720
like lords and ladies of the land.

00:29:36.720 --> 00:29:40.860
We are the title holders.
That's a thing, like legally.

00:29:40.860 --> 00:29:43.410
We can't do what we want with it. (laughs)

00:29:43.410 --> 00:29:48.240
So you know, now that we've
contractually entered, sorry,

00:29:48.240 --> 00:29:51.060
now that we've entered into
a contractual obligation

00:29:51.060 --> 00:29:53.013
to specific people.

00:29:55.680 --> 00:30:00.420
The stuff that normally
let's say flows with owning

00:30:00.420 --> 00:30:02.370
or being the title holder of a plot,

00:30:02.370 --> 00:30:04.023
purely doesn't apply here.

00:30:06.540 --> 00:30:08.860
I understand what you're saying about

00:30:11.190 --> 00:30:12.680
it perhaps...

00:30:16.950 --> 00:30:20.800
I understand what you're saying about

00:30:22.440 --> 00:30:27.440
are the customers, the real
owners if you own the title.

00:30:27.960 --> 00:30:30.720
But I think the way we see it

00:30:30.720 --> 00:30:34.260
is we take our contractual
obligations extremely seriously.

00:30:34.260 --> 00:30:37.320
- Now I commend this YouTuber
for engaging in this interview

00:30:37.320 --> 00:30:38.700
and trying to do the research,

00:30:38.700 --> 00:30:39.930
and going back to the source,

00:30:39.930 --> 00:30:42.270
and actually getting
firsthand information.

00:30:42.270 --> 00:30:44.700
But even she admits that it's confusing,

00:30:44.700 --> 00:30:46.740
and that they're aware
of others being confused.

00:30:46.740 --> 00:30:48.600
And that Established
Titles needs to update

00:30:48.600 --> 00:30:50.850
the talking points
because they're confusing.

00:30:50.850 --> 00:30:52.650
- I just think that that's
probably one of the parts

00:30:52.650 --> 00:30:53.850
that's a little bit confusing.

00:30:53.850 --> 00:30:56.880
'Cause there's some people,
I mean, even people who

00:30:56.880 --> 00:30:58.830
may have purchased through myself,

00:30:58.830 --> 00:31:02.130
who has felt like, "Oh, I thought
like there might have been

00:31:02.130 --> 00:31:04.230
like even if I can't really use it,

00:31:04.230 --> 00:31:06.630
there might have been a little
bit of legitimacy behind it."

00:31:06.630 --> 00:31:08.880
- Now I've seen a lot of people
criticize Established Titles

00:31:08.880 --> 00:31:11.130
saying that if you really cared
about environmental causes,

00:31:11.130 --> 00:31:13.290
you would just skip
Established Titles altogether

00:31:13.290 --> 00:31:14.550
and donate directly.

00:31:14.550 --> 00:31:15.960
Now I'm of two minds about this.

00:31:15.960 --> 00:31:18.300
Because first of all, that's
not how charity works.

00:31:18.300 --> 00:31:19.740
Sometimes you have to throw a party

00:31:19.740 --> 00:31:21.030
that costs a million dollars

00:31:21.030 --> 00:31:23.520
to entice guests to donate $3 million.

00:31:23.520 --> 00:31:25.770
You might not like the
waste, or the inefficiency,

00:31:25.770 --> 00:31:28.680
but sometimes you need a reason
to incise people to give.

00:31:28.680 --> 00:31:29.877
And established title CEO said quote,

00:31:29.877 --> 00:31:32.370
"In the past two years, we
have done more tangible work

00:31:32.370 --> 00:31:34.320
in the preservation of
the woodlands in Scotland

00:31:34.320 --> 00:31:35.850
than anyone else to our knowledge.

00:31:35.850 --> 00:31:38.160
This includes donating to
plant over two million trees,

00:31:38.160 --> 00:31:40.740
and acquiring over
hundreds of acres of land,

00:31:40.740 --> 00:31:41.760
and contractually committing

00:31:41.760 --> 00:31:43.860
to preserve it in its natural state.

00:31:43.860 --> 00:31:44.940
This year we are slated to

00:31:44.940 --> 00:31:47.310
be Trees for the Future's
Giving Tuesday partner,

00:31:47.310 --> 00:31:49.590
matching all donations up to $50,000.

00:31:49.590 --> 00:31:51.450
It's a shame that this
attempt to cancel us

00:31:51.450 --> 00:31:53.820
will make these efforts in
the future that much harder."

00:31:53.820 --> 00:31:57.060
Okay, sure. but let's talk
about orders of magnitude here.

00:31:57.060 --> 00:31:58.260
Now, as I said before,

00:31:58.260 --> 00:32:00.720
I'm guessing that the average
card value is about $100.

00:32:00.720 --> 00:32:03.600
It costs a maximum of $1
per tree to plant a tree.

00:32:03.600 --> 00:32:06.240
So you're talking about roughly
one to 2% of the revenue

00:32:06.240 --> 00:32:07.920
of this company going to tree planting.

00:32:07.920 --> 00:32:10.410
The less than 200 acres
that Established Titles owns

00:32:10.410 --> 00:32:12.060
is roughly 0.3 square miles,

00:32:12.060 --> 00:32:15.300
not three square miles, 0.3 square miles.

00:32:15.300 --> 00:32:16.800
In a part of Scotland that doesn't see

00:32:16.800 --> 00:32:18.060
that much development anyway.

00:32:18.060 --> 00:32:19.230
So let's be real here.

00:32:19.230 --> 00:32:21.450
Established Titles is far more

00:32:21.450 --> 00:32:22.890
of a money making venture

00:32:22.890 --> 00:32:24.660
than it is an environmental charity.

00:32:24.660 --> 00:32:26.760
So is Established Titles a scam?

00:32:26.760 --> 00:32:29.220
I mean, it seems like it,
at least colloquially.

00:32:29.220 --> 00:32:31.890
A scam is defined as a
dishonest scheme, a swindle.

00:32:31.890 --> 00:32:35.580
So probably, it seems like
there's some dishonesty there.

00:32:35.580 --> 00:32:36.413
Is it illegal?

00:32:36.413 --> 00:32:39.210
Well, there are some good
arguments to that effect.

00:32:39.210 --> 00:32:41.820
And look, Established Titles
is not the only one out there.

00:32:41.820 --> 00:32:43.200
There's a million of
these different companies,

00:32:43.200 --> 00:32:46.680
highlandtitles.com,
Scotlandtitles.com, all dreck.

00:32:46.680 --> 00:32:48.000
And defenders have said it's only as much

00:32:48.000 --> 00:32:51.540
of a scam as the name a
star registries or NFTs,

00:32:51.540 --> 00:32:53.400
to which I say, "Correct."

00:32:53.400 --> 00:32:55.890
Most of those are scams as well.

00:32:55.890 --> 00:32:57.240
And the funny thing is,
on the internet everyone

00:32:57.240 --> 00:32:58.800
always screams class action lawsuit.

00:32:58.800 --> 00:33:00.690
And class action lawsuit never makes sense

00:33:00.690 --> 00:33:02.670
in the context that people think it does.

00:33:02.670 --> 00:33:04.980
But here, if people were deceived,

00:33:04.980 --> 00:33:06.120
that is exactly the kind of thing

00:33:06.120 --> 00:33:08.490
that actually would
work as a class action.

00:33:08.490 --> 00:33:11.790
Except buried in the small
print in the terms of service

00:33:11.790 --> 00:33:13.530
on establishedtitles.com is

00:33:13.530 --> 00:33:15.420
a class action arbitration waiver.

00:33:15.420 --> 00:33:16.620
Though I do question whether

00:33:16.620 --> 00:33:18.570
that would be enforceable in this context.

00:33:18.570 --> 00:33:20.250
And even if it's not outright illegal,

00:33:20.250 --> 00:33:22.440
it's terrible for creators at large.

00:33:22.440 --> 00:33:24.510
Some creators in the wake of apologizing

00:33:24.510 --> 00:33:26.940
for running an established
title sponsorship have admitted

00:33:26.940 --> 00:33:29.100
that they will basically
take any sponsorship

00:33:29.100 --> 00:33:29.970
that comes their way.

00:33:29.970 --> 00:33:32.940
- I get a sponsorship
opportunity for almost anything,

00:33:32.940 --> 00:33:33.780
I'm gonna take it.

00:33:33.780 --> 00:33:35.040
- And that's the creator's right.

00:33:35.040 --> 00:33:37.170
They can run whatever
sponsorship they want to,

00:33:37.170 --> 00:33:39.330
or decide not to run whatever
sponsorship they want to.

00:33:39.330 --> 00:33:40.380
But the thing is,

00:33:40.380 --> 00:33:42.660
it hurts the entire creator economy,

00:33:42.660 --> 00:33:45.660
because when very prominent
YouTubers promote crap,

00:33:45.660 --> 00:33:49.080
everyone assumes that all
the sponsorships are crap.

00:33:49.080 --> 00:33:50.790
And I've seen lots of
comments to the effect

00:33:50.790 --> 00:33:53.280
that the viewer just automatically assumes

00:33:53.280 --> 00:33:57.180
that everything any YouTuber
promotes is just dreck.

00:33:57.180 --> 00:33:59.307
And that's not fair to the people who

00:33:59.307 --> 00:34:01.410
are running legitimate sponsorships.

00:34:01.410 --> 00:34:04.200
And to that point, look,
my sponsors are legitimate.

00:34:04.200 --> 00:34:06.840
If I say that I use them,
I actually use them.

00:34:06.840 --> 00:34:07.920
And not to be holier than thou,

00:34:07.920 --> 00:34:09.720
but I'm represented by Nebula Talent,

00:34:09.720 --> 00:34:12.600
and full disclosure, I'm
a large minority owner.

00:34:12.600 --> 00:34:15.390
But literally no one
represented by Nebula talent ran

00:34:15.390 --> 00:34:17.280
an Established Titles sponsorship.

00:34:17.280 --> 00:34:20.550
Now fair, Established Titles
riseable was on its face,

00:34:20.550 --> 00:34:21.600
but at the same time,

00:34:21.600 --> 00:34:23.820
the CEO of Nebula Talent, Dave Whiskus,

00:34:23.820 --> 00:34:26.100
has kept telling everyone
not to burn their reputation

00:34:26.100 --> 00:34:29.010
on what was at best a
gimmick or a gag gift.

00:34:29.010 --> 00:34:30.870
Because once you lose your credibility,

00:34:30.870 --> 00:34:32.160
you never get it back.

00:34:32.160 --> 00:34:33.600
And there's not just reputational risk,

00:34:33.600 --> 00:34:34.950
there's also counterparty risk.

00:34:34.950 --> 00:34:36.450
And wouldn't should know it?

00:34:36.450 --> 00:34:38.010
Established Titles has now pulled all

00:34:38.010 --> 00:34:40.320
of their sponsorships for 2022,

00:34:40.320 --> 00:34:42.450
because of all of this backlash.

00:34:42.450 --> 00:34:45.210
They're actively breaking
contracts they had with creators,

00:34:45.210 --> 00:34:46.050
though at the same time they're

00:34:46.050 --> 00:34:48.660
also letting creators out of
their contracts if they want.

00:34:48.660 --> 00:34:51.900
So it was good while it
lasted. I hope it was worth it.

00:34:51.900 --> 00:34:53.160
But look on the bright side,

00:34:53.160 --> 00:34:54.930
